# Normalize line endings so a checkout on Windows (core.autocrlf=true is the
# Git-for-Windows default) can't corrupt files that must stay LF.
#
# Without this, a fresh clone/reset on Windows rewrites run-web.sh with CRLF and
# its shebang breaks under WSL/Linux ("bad interpreter"). The repo already stores
# LF everywhere; these rules just make that guaranteed rather than incidental.

# Let git decide text vs binary, and store text as LF in the repo.
* text=auto

# Must be LF in the working tree too -- executed by a POSIX shell.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers: keep CRLF so cmd.exe is never surprised.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
